    "author_association": "OWNER",
    "body": "BLOCKING REVIEW - Atom 5 Safari repair PR #415, head `b5288e5739ecbb27e58237f9ea2c2e4446361a6a`.\n\nThe new `tools/test_stage7_15_atom5_oleg_rendered_dom.mjs` uses `page.waitForFunction()` return values as primitive timestamps and as the Oleg battle ID. In Playwright Node, `waitForFunction` returns a `JSHandle`, not the underlying value. As currently committed:\n\n- `visibleStamp(...)` returns `page.waitForFunction(...)`, then `cardAt - greetingAt`, `resultAt - answerAt` etc. attempt arithmetic on JSHandles. That cannot establish `>= 1000 ms` and may evaluate to NaN.\n- `const olegBattleId = await page.waitForFunction(...)` stores a JSHandle; interpolating it into `[data-battle-id=\"${olegBattleId}\"]` and using it as the ID is incorrect.\n\nExtract primitives explicitly with `await handle.jsonValue()` (and dispose handles when appropriate), including before page reload. Rerun the **committed** test file in a clean checkout at exact PR head and attach the exact command/output with all four numeric DOM visibility gaps and yellow/red DOM checks. Additionally, either execute it as part of appropriate CI or provide reproducible local run evidence; current green `validate`/`capture` jobs do not execute this Chromium DOM test, as confirmed by their step lists. Preserve the 8-file focused scope and do not alter gameplay just to satisfy the test. Do not merge or claim Safari PASS until the test defect is corrected and reviewed.\n\nReference: https://playwright.dev/docs/next/api/class-page#page-wait-for-function and https://playwright.dev/docs/api/class-jshandle#js-handle-json-value.",
