    "body": "## Summary\n\n- Render all three scripted Oleg defense choices yellow before selection; preserve the hidden neutral Oleg argument and resolved red/yellow colors.\n- Start card, public-loss, and DM delays only after the corresponding UI content is present across consecutive animation frames.\n- Preserve checkpoint reload behavior, selected answer, exactly-once settlement, and generic battle colors.\n- Refresh Web/docs mirrors and cache tokens.\n\n## Validation\n\n- RED on exact main `e6f9985d5df0f7e2a26ac83dbafea214b277fd15`: rendered DOM returned three `chip hiddenPower`; timestamp test measured result-to-public-loss at 979.6 ms.\n- GREEN Chromium DOM test: visible gaps 1214/1035/1034/1019 ms; reload after answer retained selection and sequence. Generic color isolation passed.\n- Focused Oleg fake-timer/contract tests, Atom 1 and 3, Nastya, Oleg DM/escape, demo isolation/routing, reload/resume, first battle and relevant Stage 7.15 suites passed.\n- JavaScript syntax, diff check, Web/docs mirror parity passed. GitHub `validate` and both `capture` checks succeeded.\n- Four legacy scripts fail identically on clean baseline due to stale assertions: Atom 4 rematch sentinel, progressive-disclosure callback location, Rayhan branch marker, and Safari corridor marker. Safari is not tested here and remains user-owned.\n\nDo not merge. Stop at PASS_CANDIDATE for ChatGPT review and the user's later Safari acceptance.",
